WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.780
1945.

2
00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:06.090
The war ends, and a road runs
forward from there to today.

3
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:09.770
Along it, signs keep popping
up: a mushroom cloud,

4
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.770
a ship arriving, a ballot
box, a wall coming down,

5
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.260
a phone screen.

6
00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:19.780
Above the road, one figure keeps
arriving at the same closed door.

7
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.770
The sign over it is blank.

8
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.680
Decades of change.

9
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.900
So what do writers after
1945 keep returning to?

10
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:31.840
In this mission, you'll map the
dates that post-war writers answer,

11
00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.880
from the end of the war to now.

12
00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.340
You'll sort a long list of
concerns that keep coming back.

13
00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.700
And you'll learn to use
context that explains a text,

14
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:42.980
not context that decorates it.

15
00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:48.130
Your mission: find out what writers
after 1945 keep returning to.
